  "title": "Lebanon's Step Toward Ending Capital Punishment",
  "summary": "The Lebanese parliament has passed a bill to abolish the death penalty, making it the first country in the Middle East to end capital punishment. This move aims to address concerns about the legality and fairness of capital punishment in the region.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The new law would make Lebanon the first country in the Middle East to end capital punishment.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Amnesty International reports that three-quarters of the world has abolished the death penalty in law or practice.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bill would allow life imprisonment with hard labor as the highest penalty.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
